                <h1>Miami-Dade County Court Records</h1>
                <p>Miami-Dade County court records are kept by the Clerk of the Court and Comptroller in Miami, Florida. This is the most populous county in the state with close to 2.7 million people. The clerk handles civil, criminal, family, probate, and traffic case filings for all of Miami-Dade County. You can search most court records for free through the clerk's online portal or visit the courthouse at 20 NW 1st Avenue in Miami. Searching court records in Miami-Dade County takes just a few clicks from any computer or phone with web access.</p>
