                <h2>Miami-Dade Clerk of Court</h2>
                <p>Juan Fernandez-Barquin, Esq. serves as the Clerk of the Court and Comptroller for Miami-Dade County. The clerk's office runs an enhanced Online Case Search portal that gives access to civil, family, and probate court records with just a few clicks. You can also look up criminal cases through the new Criminal Justice Online Case Search and Images system, known as COIN. These tools are free for basic searches in Miami-Dade County.</p>

                <p>The main office of the <a href="https://www.miamidadeclerk.gov/">Miami-Dade Clerk of the Court</a> is at 20 NW 1st Avenue, Miami, Florida 33128. You can call 305-275-1155 for help. The clerk handles all court filings, stores case files, and gives out copies. Under <a href="https://www.leg.state.fl.us/Statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0100-0199/0119/0119.html">Florida Statute Chapter 119</a>, all court records in Miami-Dade County are public unless sealed by a judge or made confidential by law. The clerk must keep social security numbers and bank account data out of public view without anyone asking, per Florida Statute 119.0714.</p>

                <p>The clerk's office also launched a Civil Infractions Application for boating, park, and wildlife citations in Miami-Dade County. You can review, track, and pay these from home. A free Property Fraud Alert service is available to warn you if someone tries to file a false document against your property in Miami-Dade County.</p>

